character.kweebec-mage.epithet=Mage
character.kweebec-villager.name=Kweebec
dialogue.kweebec-mage.text=The roots hum tonight. Something old stirs beneath the forest.
dialogue.kweebec-mage.bye=I will keep my ears open.
quest.kweebec-mage.title=The only mage
quest.kweebec-mage.description=There is only one Kweebec mage in all the lands, and the roots speak through them. Seek them out before it is too late.
quest.kweebec-mage.short=Talk to the Kweebec mage
character.village-grandfather.epithet=Keeper of the Grandfather
dialogue.village-grandfather.intro.page1=Have you heard of the Grandfather? The first tree, the one every Kweebec grew from.
dialogue.village-grandfather.intro.page2=He is tired. His leaves fall before autumn and his sap runs slow. Only life itself can wake him.
dialogue.village-grandfather.intro.page3=Gather a hundred essences of life, bind them into one at a farming bench, and bring it to me. I will take it to him.
dialogue.village-grandfather.accept=I will wake the Grandfather.
dialogue.village-grandfather.waiting=A hundred essences, bound into one. The Grandfather can wait a little longer, but not forever.
dialogue.village-grandfather.tale.page1=Feel it? It pulses like a heart. Sit, and I will tell you why it matters.
dialogue.village-grandfather.tale.page2=Long ago, there was only the Grandfather, alone in a bare land. He dropped one seed each spring, and each seed woke as a Kweebec.
dialogue.village-grandfather.tale.page3=We planted the forests around him so he would never be alone again. Every village still keeps a tree for him.
dialogue.village-grandfather.tale.page4=You gave him a spring he did not have. Take these seeds that never die, the way he never does. Choose as you like.
quest.village-grandfather.title=The Grandfather is tired
quest.village-grandfather.description=The Grandfather, the first tree of the Kweebec, is weakening. Only concentrated life can wake him.
quest.village-grandfather.short=Make a concentrated essence of life and bring it to the keeper of the Grandfather
quest.village-grandfather.gather.title=Gather 100 essences of life
quest.village-grandfather.craft.title=Craft a concentrated essence of life
quest.village-grandfather.give.title=Give it to the keeper of the Grandfather

# Village stories
dialogue.village.decline=Not right now.
dialogue.village.give=Here you go.
dialogue.village.later=Not yet.
dialogue.village.bye=Take care.
dialogue.village.trade=Show me your wares.
character.village-snack.epithet=Hungry sapling
dialogue.village-snack.intro.page1=The carrots in the garden are finally ripe, I can smell them from here! But I'm not allowed to pick them on my own.
dialogue.village-snack.intro.page2=Would you pick one for me? Just one. A crunchy one.
dialogue.village-snack.accept=I'll pick one for you.
dialogue.village-snack.waiting=Is it crunchy? Is it? Let me see!
dialogue.village-snack.thanks=Crunch! Best carrot of the whole season. Don't tell the farmer.
quest.village-snack.title=A crunchy snack
quest.village-snack.description=A hungry little sapling has been eyeing the garden carrots all morning, but it is not allowed to pick them itself.
quest.village-snack.short=Pick a ripe carrot in the village and bring it to the young Kweebec
quest.village-snack.harvest.title=Pick a ripe carrot
quest.village-snack.give.title=Give the carrot to the young Kweebec
character.village-lantern.epithet=Little carver
dialogue.village-lantern.intro.page1=Tonight is lantern night! Everyone carves a pumpkin, and mine will be the biggest. The biggest!
dialogue.village-lantern.intro.page2=Only... the grown-ups won't let me near the patch with a knife. Could you pick a ripe pumpkin for me?
dialogue.village-lantern.accept=A big one, coming up.
dialogue.village-lantern.waiting=Is it big? Bigger than my head? It has to be bigger than my head.
dialogue.village-lantern.thanks=Look at it glow! Everyone will see my lantern from the other side of the village.
quest.village-lantern.title=A pumpkin for lantern night
quest.village-lantern.description=A young sapling wants to carve the biggest lantern of the village, but the grown-ups keep it away from the pumpkin patch.
quest.village-lantern.short=Pick a ripe pumpkin in the village and bring it to the young Kweebec
quest.village-lantern.harvest.title=Pick a ripe pumpkin
quest.village-lantern.give.title=Give the pumpkin to the young Kweebec
character.village-doll.epithet=Teary sapling
dialogue.village-doll.intro.page1=My doll Bramble lost all her stuffing. She's flat as a leaf now.
dialogue.village-doll.intro.page2=Cotton grows in the garden. If you bring me three fluffy ones, I can make her round again.
dialogue.village-doll.accept=Three cotton, for Bramble.
dialogue.village-doll.waiting=Bramble is waiting too. She's very patient, for a flat doll.
dialogue.village-doll.thanks=She's round again! Bramble says thank you. Well, I say it for her.
quest.village-doll.title=A doll full of cotton
quest.village-doll.description=A little sapling's favourite doll lost its stuffing, and the cotton in the village garden is ripe.
quest.village-doll.short=Pick 3 ripe cotton in the village and bring them to the young Kweebec
quest.village-doll.harvest.title=Pick 3 ripe cotton
quest.village-doll.give.title=Give the cotton to the young Kweebec
character.village-mushroom.epithet=Shy sapling
dialogue.village-mushroom.intro.page1=The others dared me to bring back a mushroom from the old trees. But they're so tall and dark...
dialogue.village-mushroom.intro.page2=If you pick one, I'll tell them I was very brave. You were very brave. We were brave together.
dialogue.village-mushroom.accept=We'll be brave together.
dialogue.village-mushroom.waiting=Did you find one? Was it scary? Don't tell me if it was scary.
dialogue.village-mushroom.thanks=They didn't believe me at first. Then they saw the mushroom. Now I'm the bravest!
dialogue.village-mushroom.absent=The old trees are bare. Somebody picked every mushroom... I am not sad. A little relieved, maybe.
dialogue.village-mushroom.giveup=There is not a single mushroom left around here.
quest.village-mushroom.title=The bravest mushroom
quest.village-mushroom.description=The village children dared a shy sapling to bring back a mushroom from the old trees. It would rather not go alone.
quest.village-mushroom.short=Pick a mushroom and bring it to the young Kweebec
quest.village-mushroom.harvest.title=Pick a mushroom
quest.village-mushroom.give.title=Give the mushroom to the young Kweebec
character.village-spiders.epithet=Sleepless sapling
dialogue.village-spiders.intro.page1=Something scratches under my house every night. Click, click, click. I saw legs. Too many legs.
dialogue.village-spiders.intro.page2=There are spiders all around the village. Could you squash three of them? Then I could finally sleep.
dialogue.village-spiders.accept=I'll take care of the spiders.
dialogue.village-spiders.absent=Last night something scratched under my house. It's quiet now... maybe it's gone. Maybe.
dialogue.village-spiders.waiting=I can still hear them. Click, click. Please hurry.
dialogue.village-spiders.giveup=I can't find any spiders around here.
dialogue.village-spiders.thanks=No more clicking! I slept all night. Here, the silk they left behind, and an antidote in case one bit you.
quest.village-spiders.title=The monster under the house
quest.village-spiders.description=A young Kweebec hears spiders scratching under its house every night and cannot sleep anymore.
quest.village-spiders.short=Kill 3 spiders near the village
character.village-blade.epithet=Would-be guard
dialogue.village-blade.intro.page1=One day I'll be a Razorleaf, like my big sister. But a Razorleaf needs a blade, and they won't give me one.
dialogue.village-blade.intro.page2=If you make me a sword, even a crude one, I can start training. I'll give you my savings!
dialogue.village-blade.accept=I'll make you a sword.
dialogue.village-blade.waiting=I've been training with a stick. The stick lost.
dialogue.village-blade.thanks=Hyah! Hyah! Watch out, Trorks! Here, my savings. I won't need them now, I have a sword.
character.village-outlander-map.epithet=Watchful guard
dialogue.village-outlander-map.intro.page1=A week ago, Outlander scouts circled the village at dusk. One of them was drawing on a scrap of leather. Then they vanished.
dialogue.village-outlander-map.intro.page2=I think they're mapping our defences. If you ever face Outlanders, search them for that map. I need to know what they saw.
dialogue.village-outlander-map.accept=I'll find that map.
dialogue.village-outlander-map.waiting=I've doubled the night watch. Nobody likes me much right now.
dialogue.village-outlander-map.thanks=Our gates, our wells, the gap in the east hedge... they saw everything. Now we know where to build. Take these, you've earned the guard's thanks.
quest.village-outlander-map.title=The Outlanders' map
quest.village-outlander-map.description=Outlander scouts were seen mapping a Kweebec village a week ago before disappearing. A guard wants that map to learn what they saw.
quest.village-outlander-map.short=Take the old map from Outlanders and bring it to the Kweebec guard
quest.village-outlander-map.loot.title=Take the map from Outlanders
quest.village-outlander-map.give.title=Bring the map to the Kweebec guard
quest.village-blade.title=A blade fit for a Razorleaf
quest.village-blade.description=A young Kweebec dreams of joining the village guard, but nobody will trust it with a blade yet.
character.village-silk-loom.epithet=Idle weaver
dialogue.village-silk-loom.intro.page1=Spiders got into my workshop a few days ago. They wrapped up my three bolts of silk and dragged them off to who knows where.
dialogue.village-silk-loom.intro.page2=My loom can't wait forever. If you hunt spiders, check their webs for my silk. I'll weave you something fine with it.
dialogue.village-silk-loom.accept=I'll get your silk back.
dialogue.village-silk-loom.waiting=My loom just sits there. I've started weaving grass. It's not the same.
dialogue.village-silk-loom.thanks=Three bolts, barely chewed! Choose a piece, I'll weave it for you right now.
quest.village-silk-loom.title=Silk for the loom
quest.village-silk-loom.description=Spiders raided a young Kweebec weaver's workshop and dragged off its bolts of silk, leaving its loom idle.
quest.village-silk-loom.short=Take 3 bolts of silk back from spiders and bring them to the Kweebec weaver
quest.village-silk-loom.loot.title=Take the silk back from spiders
quest.village-silk-loom.give.title=Bring the silk to the Kweebec weaver
quest.village-blade.short=Craft a crude sword and give it to the young Kweebec
character.village-looted-cart.epithet=Robbed trader
dialogue.village-looted-cart.intro.page1=My cart! Goblins ambushed it on the road last week and ran off with three crates of my best goods.
dialogue.village-looted-cart.intro.page2=They scattered into the wild before anyone could follow. Bring my crates back if you ever catch goblins, and you can pick something from them.
dialogue.village-looted-cart.accept=I'll bring your crates back.
dialogue.village-looted-cart.waiting=Three crates. Silver, potions, powder. I count them in my sleep.
dialogue.village-looted-cart.thanks=My crates, still sealed! Go on, take your pick from what's inside, you've earned it.
quest.village-looted-cart.title=The looted cart
quest.village-looted-cart.description=Goblins ambushed a Kweebec merchant's cart on the road and made off with three crates of goods before vanishing into the wild.
quest.village-looted-cart.short=Take 3 wooden crates back from goblins and bring them to the Kweebec merchant
quest.village-looted-cart.loot.title=Take the crates back from goblins
quest.village-looted-cart.give.title=Bring the crates to the Kweebec merchant
character.village-wheat.epithet=Little baker
dialogue.village-wheat.intro.page1=I want to bake my first loaf all by myself. From the very first seed!
dialogue.village-wheat.intro.page2=But I'm too small to dig the rows. Will you plant these wheat seeds in the tilled soil around here?
dialogue.village-wheat.accept=Let's start your loaf.
dialogue.village-wheat.waiting=Is it growing yet? Bread takes so long...
dialogue.village-wheat.thanks=Real wheat, my wheat! The first loaf will be yours. Here, some flour to start.
quest.village-wheat.title=The very first loaf
quest.village-wheat.description=A sproutling wants to bake its first loaf from the very first seed, but is too small to dig.
quest.village-wheat.short=Plant 4 wheat seeds near the young Kweebec in the village
quest.village-blade.craft.title=Craft a crude sword
quest.village-blade.give.title=Give the sword to the young Kweebec
character.village-sleepy-guard.epithet=Ashamed guard
dialogue.village-sleepy-guard.intro.page1=Psst. Keep your voice down. A week ago I fell asleep on watch, and a band of Trorks walked off with three of our spears.
dialogue.village-sleepy-guard.intro.page2=They're long gone, nobody knows where. If you ever cross Trorks, take the spears back for me. Nobody must know.
dialogue.village-sleepy-guard.accept=Your secret is safe. I'll find them.
dialogue.village-sleepy-guard.waiting=The captain counts the rack every morning. I keep standing in front of the gap.
dialogue.village-sleepy-guard.thanks=All three! Back on the rack before the captain's count. Take my own spare spear, and the iron I'd set aside to replace them.
quest.village-sleepy-guard.title=The guard who fell asleep
quest.village-sleepy-guard.description=A Kweebec guard fell asleep on watch a week ago, and Trorks stole three spears from the rack. It wants them back before anyone notices.
quest.village-sleepy-guard.short=Take 3 crude spears back from Trorks and return them to the Kweebec guard
quest.village-sleepy-guard.loot.title=Take the spears back from Trorks
quest.village-sleepy-guard.give.title=Return the spears to the Kweebec guard
character.village-dull-blade.epithet=Weary guard
dialogue.village-dull-blade.intro.page1=My leaf blade has gone dull, and the binding on the hilt is coming apart. I can't leave my post to fix it.
dialogue.village-dull-blade.intro.page2=Bring me sap to glue it and fibre to bind it, and you won't regret it.
dialogue.village-dull-blade.accept=I'll bring sap and fibre.
dialogue.village-dull-blade.waiting=Still on watch. Still with a dull blade.
dialogue.village-dull-blade.thanks=Sharp as a thorn again. Take these, spares from my kit. The guard looks after those who look after the guard.
quest.village-dull-blade.title=Leaf blade gone dull
quest.village-dull-blade.description=A Kweebec guard cannot leave its post, and its leaf blade is falling apart.
quest.village-dull-blade.short=Bring 6 tree sap and 10 plant fibers to the Kweebec guard
character.village-cold-forge.epithet=Guard smith
dialogue.village-cold-forge.intro.page1=The storm flooded the charcoal shed and my forge has gone cold. No fire, no blades, and the Trorks won't wait for the sun.
dialogue.village-cold-forge.intro.page2=Bring me logs to feed the fire and iron to work, and the first thing out of the forge is yours.
dialogue.village-cold-forge.accept=Logs and iron, coming.
dialogue.village-cold-forge.waiting=The anvil is cold to the touch. I hate that.
dialogue.village-cold-forge.thanks=Hear that? The forge sings again. Here, as promised. Pick the one that suits your hand.
quest.village-cold-forge.title=The cold forge
quest.village-cold-forge.description=A storm flooded the guard's charcoal shed, and the forge that keeps the village blades sharp has gone cold.
quest.village-cold-forge.short=Bring 3 iron ingots and 10 logs to the Kweebec smith
character.village-skeletons.epithet=Outnumbered guard
dialogue.village-skeletons.intro.page1=Skeletons keep wandering out of the woods, day and night. The patrol can't watch every path.
dialogue.village-skeletons.intro.page2=Some are close right now. Break three of them before they reach the houses.
dialogue.village-skeletons.accept=I'll break them.
dialogue.village-skeletons.absent=No rattling in the woods today. Enjoy it while it lasts.
dialogue.village-skeletons.waiting=I can still hear bones rattling between the trees.
dialogue.village-skeletons.giveup=I can't find any skeletons around here.
dialogue.village-skeletons.thanks=Three fewer bone heaps on our paths. Take this, a guard's pay.
quest.village-skeletons.title=Rattling in the woods
quest.village-skeletons.description=A Kweebec guard cannot hold back alone the skeletons wandering out of the woods.
quest.village-skeletons.short=Kill 3 skeletons near the village
character.village-ingredients.epithet=Young alchemist
dialogue.village-ingredients.intro.page1=A little one has a fever and my shelves are empty. I need wild berries and red petals for a healing brew.
dialogue.village-ingredients.intro.page2=Bring them and I'll brew enough for the little one, and for you.
dialogue.village-ingredients.accept=I'll gather them.
dialogue.village-ingredients.waiting=The fever hasn't broken yet. Hurry, if you can.
dialogue.village-ingredients.thanks=The little one is sleeping soundly. Your share of the batch, and something for the road.
quest.village-ingredients.title=Short of ingredients
quest.village-ingredients.description=A young Kweebec alchemist must brew a remedy for a feverish child, but its shelves are bare.
quest.village-ingredients.short=Bring 12 wild berries and 6 red petals to the Kweebec alchemist
character.village-broken-still.epithet=Unlucky alchemist
dialogue.village-broken-still.intro.page1=Crack! My still split right down the middle this morning. Weeks of work, gone.
dialogue.village-broken-still.intro.page2=The guard needs healing potions before nightfall. Could you brew two at an alchemy bench? I'll pay you properly, it's hard work.
dialogue.village-broken-still.accept=I'll brew them.
dialogue.village-broken-still.waiting=I tried tying the still together with roots. It did not go well.
dialogue.village-broken-still.thanks=Perfect colour, perfect smell. You have the touch! Here, iron and essence, you've earned them.
quest.village-broken-still.title=The broken still
quest.village-broken-still.description=A Kweebec alchemist's still cracked just when the guard needs healing potions.
quest.village-broken-still.short=Brew 2 lesser health potions and give them to the Kweebec alchemist
quest.village-broken-still.craft.title=Brew 2 lesser health potions
quest.village-broken-still.give.title=Give the potions to the alchemist
dialogue.village-seeds.intro.page1=Mice got into my seed sack over the winter. Not a single seed left, and planting season is here.
dialogue.village-seeds.intro.page2=Two seed bags each of carrot, lettuce and pumpkin, that's all I need to start again.
dialogue.village-seeds.accept=I'll find you some seeds.
quest.village-seeds.title=Seeds for {giver}
quest.village-seeds.description=Mice emptied a Kweebec farmer's seed sack, right at planting time.
quest.village-seeds.short=Bring 2 carrot, 2 lettuce and 2 pumpkin seed bags to {giver}
character.village-big-scythe.epithet=Tiny harvester
dialogue.village-big-scythe.intro.page1=My big brother left me in charge of the wheat. But the scythe is taller than me!
dialogue.village-big-scythe.intro.page2=The wheat is ripe. Could you cut 5 sheaves and bring them here before he comes back?
dialogue.village-big-scythe.accept=I'll cut them.
dialogue.village-big-scythe.absent=My brother said to watch the wheat. It's not ripe yet, so I'm watching.
dialogue.village-big-scythe.waiting=Hurry! If he comes back and the wheat isn't cut...
dialogue.village-big-scythe.giveup=There's no ripe wheat left around here.
dialogue.village-big-scythe.thanks=Five sheaves! He'll think I did it all myself. Take this, and not a word.
quest.village-big-scythe.title=A scythe too tall
quest.village-big-scythe.description=A sproutling left in charge of the wheat cannot lift the scythe.
quest.village-big-scythe.short=Harvest 5 ripe wheat near the young Kweebec and bring it back
quest.village-big-scythe.harvest.title=Harvest 5 ripe wheat
quest.village-big-scythe.give.title=Give the wheat to the young Kweebec
dialogue.village-ruined-harvest.intro.page1=Boars came through the fields last night. They trampled everything they didn't eat.
dialogue.village-ruined-harvest.intro.page2=The village eats from my rows. Please, gather what's still ripe in the gardens and bring it to me, so nobody goes hungry.
dialogue.village-ruined-harvest.accept=I'll gather what's left.
quest.village-ruined-harvest.title={giver}'s ruined harvest
quest.village-ruined-harvest.description=Boars ravaged a Kweebec farmer's fields, and the whole village depends on his harvest.
quest.village-ruined-harvest.short=Harvest 4 carrots, 2 lettuces and 2 pumpkins in the village and bring them to {giver}
quest.village-ruined-harvest.harvestcarrots.title=Pick 4 ripe carrots
quest.village-ruined-harvest.harvestlettuces.title=Pick 2 ripe lettuces
quest.village-ruined-harvest.harvestpumpkins.title=Pick 2 ripe pumpkins
quest.village-ruined-harvest.give.title=Give the harvest to {giver}
character.village-empty-pot.epithet=Young cook
dialogue.village-empty-pot.intro.page1=The guards' stew went sour in the sun. Sour! I can't serve them sour stew.
dialogue.village-empty-pot.intro.page2=Mushrooms make the best broth. Six of them and I can start over.
dialogue.village-empty-pot.accept=Six mushrooms, coming up.
dialogue.village-empty-pot.waiting=The pot is empty and the guards are hungry. They're grumpy when they're hungry.
dialogue.village-empty-pot.thanks=Smell that! Here, skewers fresh off the fire, and my best recipe. Don't share it with the cook next door.
quest.village-empty-pot.title=The empty pot
quest.village-empty-pot.description=The guards' stew spoiled in the sun, and a young Kweebec cook has nothing left to put in the pot.
quest.village-empty-pot.short=Bring 6 mushrooms to the Kweebec cook
character.village-chillies.epithet=Daredevil taster
dialogue.village-chillies.intro.page1=The guards say no Kweebec can eat a whole chilli without crying. I will prove them wrong.
dialogue.village-chillies.intro.page2=First I need chillies. Plant these in the tilled soil around here for me?
dialogue.village-chillies.accept=I'll plant them.
dialogue.village-chillies.waiting=I'm training. I licked a pepper leaf this morning. Didn't cry. Much.
dialogue.village-chillies.thanks=Chilli rows! Soon the guards will see. Here, something warm for your trouble.
quest.village-chillies.title=No tears
quest.village-chillies.description=A Kweebec wants to prove it can eat a whole chilli without crying, but first needs to grow some.
quest.village-chillies.short=Plant 4 chilli seeds near the young Kweebec in the village
character.village-pies.epithet=Busy baker
dialogue.village-pies.intro.page1=The night watch eats more pie than I can bake. Every evening, the same hungry faces.
dialogue.village-pies.intro.page2=Bring me two dough and two pumpkins, and I'll teach you how I make mine.
dialogue.village-pies.accept=Dough and pumpkins it is.
dialogue.village-pies.waiting=The oven is warm. The guards are warmer. Impatient, I mean.
dialogue.village-pies.thanks=Two pies for you, fresh from the oven, and my recipe. Now you can feed your own night watch.
quest.village-pies.title=Pies for the night watch
quest.village-pies.description=A Kweebec baker cannot keep up with the appetite of the village night watch.
quest.village-pies.short=Bring 2 dough and 2 pumpkins to the Kweebec baker
character.village-snakes.epithet=Jumpy sapling
dialogue.village-snakes.intro.page1=Something slid over my feet while I was gathering reeds. Cold, scaly, and it hissed at me!
dialogue.village-snakes.intro.page2=The marsh is full of snakes this season. Could you get rid of three of them? I need those reeds.
dialogue.village-snakes.accept=I'll deal with the snakes.
dialogue.village-snakes.absent=Not a single hiss in the reeds today. I'll gather while I can.
dialogue.village-snakes.waiting=Every rustle in the reeds makes me jump. Are they gone yet?
dialogue.village-snakes.giveup=I can't find any snakes around here.
dialogue.village-snakes.thanks=No more hissing in the reeds! Here, antidotes, better safe than bitten. And the skins they shed.
quest.village-snakes.title=Hissing in the reeds
quest.village-snakes.description=A young Kweebec no longer dares gather reeds in the marsh, where snakes hide.
quest.village-snakes.short=Kill 3 snakes near the village
character.village-drying-rack.epithet=Grumpy tanner
dialogue.village-drying-rack.intro.page1=A boar charged through my yard and rolled in every hide on the rack. Every single one, ruined.
dialogue.village-drying-rack.intro.page2=Hunt a few boars and bring me four good hides. I'll tan them all for you, and add some light leather for your trouble.
dialogue.village-drying-rack.accept=I'll hunt some boars.
dialogue.village-drying-rack.waiting=I can still smell that boar. The whole yard smells of boar.
dialogue.village-drying-rack.thanks=Good thick hides. There, tanned and ready, and the light leather as promised.
quest.village-drying-rack.title=The trampled drying rack
quest.village-drying-rack.description=A boar wrecked a Kweebec tanner's drying rack and every hide on it.
quest.village-drying-rack.short=Hunt 3 boars and bring 4 medium hides to the Kweebec tanner
quest.village-drying-rack.hunt.title=Hunt 3 boars
quest.village-drying-rack.give.title=Give 4 medium hides to the tanner
character.village-bandages.epithet=Village healer
dialogue.village-bandages.intro.page1=The night watch came back scratched and bruised again. I've used my last bandage.
dialogue.village-bandages.intro.page2=Bandages are simple: fibre and sap. Make me three? My hands are full with the patients.
dialogue.village-bandages.accept=Three bandages, right away.
dialogue.village-bandages.waiting=Hold still, you! Not you. The guard.
dialogue.village-bandages.thanks=Just in time. Take these, I keep them for emergencies, and you were one.
quest.village-bandages.title=Bandages for the night watch
quest.village-bandages.description=The village healer ran out of bandages, and the night watch keeps coming back hurt.
quest.village-bandages.short=Craft 3 bandages and give them to the Kweebec healer
quest.village-bandages.craft.title=Craft 3 bandages
quest.village-bandages.give.title=Give the bandages to the healer
dialogue.village-burrows.intro.page1=Foxes prowl around the burrows every night. My rabbits are too scared to come out and eat.
dialogue.village-burrows.intro.page2=Chase off one of those foxes, the others will get the message. Then bring five carrots from the garden. My rabbits will love them.
dialogue.village-burrows.accept=I'll deal with the foxes.
quest.village-burrows.title=Foxes at {giver}'s burrows
quest.village-burrows.description=Foxes keep a Kweebec farmer's rabbits from leaving their burrows.
quest.village-burrows.short=Hunt 1 fox, then bring 5 carrots from the village to {giver}
quest.village-burrows.hunt.title=Hunt 1 fox
quest.village-burrows.harvest.title=Pick 5 ripe carrots
quest.village-burrows.give.title=Give the carrots to {giver}
character.village-display.epithet=Clumsy merchant
dialogue.village-display.intro.page1=A cart tipped over right onto my stall. Salads everywhere, and the customers are coming.
character.village-temple-trade.epithet=Merchant with a far client
dialogue.village-temple-trade.intro.page1=My old master, Ginkel, withdrew to the Forgotten Temple, as our elders do when they reach the age of wisdom. The trees there are sacred: nobody takes a single drop of their sap.
dialogue.village-temple-trade.intro.page2=So I send him some. His order is ready, but I can't leave my stall. Will you carry these 8 jars of sap to him?
dialogue.village-temple-trade.accept=I'll carry them to Ginkel.
dialogue.village-temple-trade.waiting=Ginkel keeps the stall of the Forgotten Temple. Mind the goblins on the way.
dialogue.village-temple-trade.thanks=The essence of the sacred tree... Ginkel has not forgotten his student. Take these 10 silver bars, you earned them on the road.
quest.village-temple-trade.title=A delivery to the temple
quest.village-temple-trade.description=A Kweebec merchant sends sap to Ginkel, his old master who withdrew to the Forgotten Temple, where nobody touches the sacred trees.
quest.village-temple-trade.short=Bring 8 tree sap to Ginkel in the Forgotten Temple
dialogue.village-temple-trade.return-waiting=Did Ginkel give you the essence of the sacred tree? Bring it back to me, I will keep it close.
quest.village-temple-trade-return.title=The essence of the sacred tree
quest.village-temple-trade-return.description=In return for the sap, Ginkel sends his old student the life essence of the temple's sacred tree, gathered without harming it.
quest.village-temple-trade-return.short=Bring the concentrated life essence back to the village Kweebec merchant
dialogue.village-display.intro.page2=Make me two wild berry salads at a cooking bench? I'll pay you in recipes, I have plenty of those.
dialogue.village-display.accept=Two salads, coming up.
dialogue.village-display.waiting=I put a cloth over the mess. Nobody noticed. Probably.
dialogue.village-display.thanks=The stall looks better than before! As promised, a recipe, and spices to go with it.
quest.village-display.title=The crushed display
quest.village-display.description=A cart crashed into a Kweebec merchant's stall just before the customers arrive.
quest.village-display.short=Make 2 wild berry salads and give them to the Kweebec merchant
character.village-heavy-pumpkins.epithet=Strained farmer
dialogue.village-heavy-pumpkins.intro.page1=These pumpkins grew bigger than me this year. I tried to lift one and it lifted me.
dialogue.village-heavy-pumpkins.intro.page2=Could you pick 2 ripe ones and carry them here? You look stronger than a sproutling.
dialogue.village-heavy-pumpkins.accept=I'll carry them.
dialogue.village-heavy-pumpkins.absent=No ripe pumpkins yet. My arms are relieved.
dialogue.village-heavy-pumpkins.waiting=Lift with the legs, they say. I don't have much of either.
dialogue.village-heavy-pumpkins.giveup=There are no ripe pumpkins left around here.
dialogue.village-heavy-pumpkins.thanks=Two pumpkins, and you are still standing! Here, the first pie is yours.
quest.village-heavy-pumpkins.title=Heavier than me
quest.village-heavy-pumpkins.description=A sproutling grew pumpkins too heavy for it to carry.
quest.village-heavy-pumpkins.short=Pick 2 ripe pumpkins near the young Kweebec and bring them back
quest.village-heavy-pumpkins.harvest.title=Pick 2 ripe pumpkins
quest.village-heavy-pumpkins.give.title=Give the pumpkins to the young Kweebec
quest.village-display.craft.title=Make 2 wild berry salads
quest.village-display.give.title=Give the salads to the merchant
dialogue.village-replant.intro.page1=The first frost is coming, and half my carrot rows are still bare.
character.klops-gentleman.epithet=Underground gentleman
dialogue.klops-gentleman.text=Pumpkins, grown under the open sky? How exotic. Down here we have salt, spices, and very good manners.
character.village-spices.epithet=Merchant out of spices
dialogue.village-spices.intro.page1=No spices left, and no salt either. The Klops gentlemen who live deep in the caves have plenty, but they never come up.
dialogue.village-spices.intro.page2=They are said to adore pumpkins. Find one of them, offer him 4 pumpkins, and bring me back 5 salt and 5 spices. I will make it worth the trip.
dialogue.village-spices.accept=I'll find a Klops gentleman.
dialogue.village-spices.waiting=The Klops gentlemen live deep underground. Bring a torch, and your best manners.
dialogue.village-spices.thanks=Salt and spices, at last! My pies will taste of something again.
quest.village-spices.title=Spices from the deep
quest.village-spices.description=A Kweebec merchant has run out of salt and spices, which only the Klops gentlemen of the deep caves trade.
quest.village-spices.short=Trade 4 pumpkins with a Klops gentleman in the caves and bring 5 salt and 5 spices to the Kweebec merchant
quest.village-spices.pumpkins.title=Give 4 pumpkins to a Klops gentleman in the caves
quest.village-spices.give.title=Give 5 salt and 5 spices to the Kweebec merchant
dialogue.village-replant.intro.page2=Here are some seeds. Plant them in the tilled soil around me, and the village will eat this winter.
dialogue.village-replant.accept=I'll plant them.
quest.village-replant.title=Before the frost, for {giver}
quest.village-replant.description=A Kweebec farmer races the first frost to sow the last rows of carrots.
quest.village-replant.short=Plant 4 carrot seeds near {giver}
dialogue.village-scarecrow.intro.page1=The crows have stopped fearing my scarecrow. One of them is nesting in its hat.
dialogue.village-scarecrow.intro.page2=Could you make me a new one and set it up in my field? A proper one, with a pumpkin head.
dialogue.village-scarecrow.accept=I'll make you a scarecrow.
quest.village-scarecrow.title=A scarecrow for {giver}
quest.village-scarecrow.description=The crows no longer fear a Kweebec farmer's old scarecrow.
quest.village-scarecrow.short=Make a scarecrow and set it up near {giver}
quest.village-scarecrow.craft.title=Make a scarecrow
quest.village-scarecrow.place.title=Set up the scarecrow near {giver}
character.village-broken-hoe.epithet=Clumsy farmer
dialogue.village-broken-hoe.intro.page1=I hit a stone and my hoe snapped in two. The stone is fine, thank you for asking.
dialogue.village-broken-hoe.intro.page2=Could you make me a copper hoe? I promise to aim for the soil this time.
dialogue.village-broken-hoe.accept=I'll make you a hoe.
dialogue.village-broken-hoe.waiting=I tried digging with a spoon. The field won.
dialogue.village-broken-hoe.thanks=A copper hoe! The stones had better watch out. Here, for your trouble.
quest.village-broken-hoe.title=The snapped hoe
quest.village-broken-hoe.description=A clumsy sproutling broke its hoe on a stone, right in the middle of the field.
quest.village-broken-hoe.short=Make a copper hoe and give it to the young Kweebec
quest.village-broken-hoe.craft.title=Make a copper hoe
quest.village-broken-hoe.give.title=Give the hoe to the young Kweebec
dialogue.village-watering-can.intro.page1=The bucket you brought me is fine at the well, but by the time I reach the garden, I'm only watering my feet.
dialogue.village-watering-can.intro.page2=Could you make me a watering can? A real one, with no holes in it.
dialogue.village-watering-can.accept=I'll make you a watering can.
quest.village-watering-can.title=A watering can for {giver}
quest.village-watering-can.description=A Kweebec farmer spills half his water between the well and the garden.
quest.village-watering-can.short=Make a watering can and give it to {giver}
quest.village-watering-can.craft.title=Make a watering can
quest.village-watering-can.give.title=Give the watering can to {giver}
dialogue.village-soggy-hay.intro.page1=The rain soaked every bale in my barn. It smells like a swamp in there now.
dialogue.village-soggy-hay.intro.page2=Could you bind 2 fresh hay bales and bring them to me? Before the next storm, ideally.
dialogue.village-soggy-hay.accept=I'll bring you hay.
quest.village-soggy-hay.title=Dry hay for {giver}
quest.village-soggy-hay.description=The rain soaked every hay bale in a Kweebec farmer's barn.
quest.village-soggy-hay.short=Make 2 hay bales and give them to {giver}
quest.village-soggy-hay.craft.title=Make 2 hay bales
quest.village-soggy-hay.give.title=Give the hay bales to {giver}
character.village-snails.epithet=Outpaced farmer
dialogue.village-snails.intro.page1=The snails reach my lettuces before I do. Every single morning.
dialogue.village-snails.intro.page2=Could you pick 3 ripe ones before they get there? I'll keep the snails talking.
dialogue.village-snails.accept=I'll pick them.
dialogue.village-snails.absent=No ripe lettuces yet. The snails and I are both waiting.
dialogue.village-snails.waiting=Hurry, I think the snails heard us.
dialogue.village-snails.giveup=There are no ripe lettuces left around here.
dialogue.village-snails.thanks=Three whole lettuces, and not a single bite! Here, you earned this.
quest.village-snails.title=Faster than snails
quest.village-snails.description=Snails reach a sproutling's lettuces before it does.
quest.village-snails.short=Pick 3 ripe lettuces near the young Kweebec and bring them back
quest.village-snails.harvest.title=Pick 3 ripe lettuces
quest.village-snails.give.title=Give the lettuces to the young Kweebec
character.farmer.epithet=Village farmer
dialogue.farmer.bring-hoe.intro.page1=My hoe split in two this morning. Without it I scratch the soil with my fingers, and the soil wins.
dialogue.farmer.bring-hoe.intro.page2=Bring me 4 logs and 3 stones, any kind, and I'll carve a new one at the bench.
dialogue.farmer.bring-bucket.intro.page1=My bucket leaks so much I reach the garden with a bucket of air. Plants don't drink air.
dialogue.farmer.bring-bucket.intro.page2=Bring me 3 pieces of wood and 1 iron bar, and I'll make myself a new one.
dialogue.farmer.bring.accept=I'll bring them.
quest.farmer.bring-hoe.title=A hoe for {giver}
quest.farmer.bring-hoe.description=A Kweebec farmer's hoe split, and it needs what it takes to carve a new one.
quest.farmer.bring-hoe.short=Bring 4 logs and 3 stones to {giver}
quest.farmer.bring-bucket.title=A bucket for {giver}
quest.farmer.bring-bucket.description=A Kweebec farmer's bucket leaks everywhere, and its plants are thirsty.
quest.farmer.bring-bucket.short=Bring 3 wood and 1 iron bar to {giver}
dialogue.farmer.harvest-aubergine.intro.page1=My aubergines are ripe, and my back is not what it was. Every row I bend over takes me a day to straighten up from.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-aubergine.intro.page2=Could you pick one for me, here around my garden?
dialogue.farmer.harvest-pumpkin.intro.page1=The pumpkins are ready, all at once, as usual. I can't pick them faster than they rot.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-pumpkin.intro.page2=Pick one for me, here around my garden? I won't forget it.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-cauliflower.intro.page1=My cauliflowers are ripe, and the rabbits noticed before I did. Every night a few more heads go missing.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-cauliflower.intro.page2=Pick 2 of them for me, here around my garden, before the rabbits get the rest?
dialogue.farmer.harvest-carrot.intro.page1=My carrots are ready, and they hold on to the soil as if they liked it down there.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-carrot.intro.page2=Pull 2 of them for me, here around my garden? Firmly, they won't come politely.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-cotton.intro.page1=The cotton is ripe, all white and fluffy. Every time I pick it, I sneeze, and the wind takes half of it.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-cotton.intro.page2=Pick 2 for me, here around my garden? I'll stay over there, far from the fluff.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-lettuce.intro.page1=My lettuces are ready, and the snails know it. I count fewer leaves every morning.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-lettuce.intro.page2=Pick one for me, here around my garden, before the snails finish it?
dialogue.farmer.harvest-onion.intro.page1=Every time I pull an onion, my eyes flood. I can't see a thing, and I trampled half the rows last time.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-onion.intro.page2=One is ripe now. Could you pull it for me, here around my garden?
dialogue.farmer.harvest-potato.intro.page1=Last time I dug up a potato, a worm wriggled out with it. A big one. It looked at me.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-potato.intro.page2=The potatoes are ripe, but I can't. Would you dig up 3 for me, here around my garden?
dialogue.farmer.harvest-wheat.intro.page1=The wheat is golden and the miller is waiting. My sickle and I are not as quick as we used to be.
dialogue.farmer.harvest-wheat.intro.page2=Cut 2 sheaves for me, here around my garden?
dialogue.farmer.tier1.accept=I'll pick them.
dialogue.farmer.bare-garden=Nothing is ripe in my garden yet. Come back when the crops are ready, I'll need a hand then.
dialogue.farmer.tier1.accepted=Thank you! I'll stay around here, come back to me once you have what it takes.
dialogue.farmer.tier1.waiting=The garden won't wait, but I can. A little.
dialogue.farmer.tier1.thanks=Thank you, friend! Thanks to you the garden is getting going again, and I have plans for it. Give me some time to sort my seeds.
dialogue.farmer.plant-potato.intro.page1=Part of the garden lies bare. Bare soil is wasted soil.
dialogue.farmer.plant-potato.intro.page2=Here are potato seeds. Would you plant 4 of them in the tilled soil around me?
dialogue.farmer.plant-onion.intro.page1=A few rows are empty, and onions keep all winter long.
dialogue.farmer.plant-onion.intro.page2=Take these onion seeds and plant 4 of them around my garden.
dialogue.farmer.plant-cauliflower.intro.page1=I promised the elder cauliflowers. I may have promised too fast.
dialogue.farmer.plant-cauliflower.intro.page2=Plant 4 of these cauliflower seeds around my garden, and I keep my word.
dialogue.farmer.tier2.accept=I'll plant them.
dialogue.farmer.tier2.accepted=Mind the rows, and thank you. I'll be right here.
dialogue.farmer.tier2.waiting=Seeds in a pocket don't grow, friend.
dialogue.farmer.tier2.thanks=You helped me get the garden going, and now the next harvest is on its way. This garden owes you a lot.
dialogue.farmer.tier3.accepted=I'll keep the garden going in the meantime. Come back when it's ready, and mind your fingers.
dialogue.farmer.tier3.waiting=A good tool takes time. A bad one takes even more, later.
dialogue.farmer.tier3.thanks=First my harvests, then my rows, and now my barn and my tools. I won't forget it, friend.
dialogue.farmer.smashed-planters.intro.page1=Something smashed every planter in my garden last night. Trorks, maybe. Whatever it was, it had big feet and no manners.
dialogue.farmer.smashed-planters.intro.page2=Remember the four I gave you? I'd buy them back, and six more if you can make them. Fifty iron bars for the ten, that's all my savings.
dialogue.farmer.smashed-planters.accept=I'll bring you ten planters.
quest.farmer.smashed-planters.title=Planters for {giver}
quest.farmer.smashed-planters.description=Something smashed a Kweebec farmer's planters overnight, and he will pay well to replace them.
quest.farmer.smashed-planters.short=Bring 10 stone planters to {giver}
dialogue.farmer.tier4.accepted=I knew I could count on you. Go, and come back to me safe.
dialogue.farmer.tier4.waiting=Every night I hear them out there. Every morning I count what's left.
dialogue.farmer.tier4.thanks=You saved more than a garden this time. Take this iron, and this essence: I kept them for the day the village would need them, and that day you were there.
dialogue.farmer.small-talk=The garden grows, I water it, and it grows some more. A good season, thanks to you.
quest.farmer.harvest-aubergine.title=Aubergines for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-aubergine.description=A Kweebec farmer's aubergines are ripe, but its back won't bend to pick them.
quest.farmer.harvest-aubergine.short=Pick a ripe aubergine near {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-pumpkin.title=Pumpkins for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-pumpkin.description=A Kweebec farmer's pumpkins all ripened at once, faster than it can pick them.
quest.farmer.harvest-pumpkin.short=Pick a ripe pumpkin near {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-cauliflower.title=Cauliflowers for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-cauliflower.description=A Kweebec farmer's cauliflowers are ripe, and the rabbits are eating them one night at a time.
quest.farmer.harvest-cauliflower.short=Pick 2 ripe cauliflowers near {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-carrot.title=Carrots for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-carrot.description=A Kweebec farmer's carrots are ripe and stubborn, and its arms are tired.
quest.farmer.harvest-carrot.short=Pull 2 ripe carrots near {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-cotton.title=Cotton for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-cotton.description=A Kweebec farmer sneezes at every cotton boll it picks.
quest.farmer.harvest-cotton.short=Pick 2 ripe cotton bolls near {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-lettuce.title=Lettuces for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-lettuce.description=A Kweebec farmer races the snails for its ripe lettuces.
quest.farmer.harvest-lettuce.short=Pick a ripe lettuce near {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-onion.title=Onions for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-onion.description=A Kweebec farmer cries so much when pulling onions that it tramples its own rows.
quest.farmer.harvest-onion.short=Pull a ripe onion near {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-potato.title=Potatoes for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-potato.description=A Kweebec farmer no longer dares dig up its potatoes since a worm looked at it.
quest.farmer.harvest-potato.short=Dig up 3 ripe potatoes near {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-wheat.title=Wheat for {giver}
quest.farmer.harvest-wheat.description=A Kweebec farmer's wheat is golden, and the miller is waiting.
quest.farmer.harvest-wheat.short=Cut 2 ripe sheaves of wheat near {giver}
quest.farmer.plant-potato.title=Potatoes for {giver}
quest.farmer.plant-potato.description=A Kweebec farmer wants its bare garden sown again.
quest.farmer.plant-potato.short=Plant 4 potato seeds near {giver}
quest.farmer.plant-onion.title=Onions for {giver}
quest.farmer.plant-onion.description=A Kweebec farmer wants onions in its emptied rows, to last the winter.
quest.farmer.plant-onion.short=Plant 4 onion seeds near {giver}
quest.farmer.plant-cauliflower.title=Cauliflowers for {giver}
quest.farmer.plant-cauliflower.description=A Kweebec farmer promised the elder cauliflowers a little too fast.
quest.farmer.plant-cauliflower.short=Plant 4 cauliflower seeds near {giver}
